  "described": {
    "alt_text": "An aerial photograph of midtown Manhattan from a glass tower, with cartoon clouds on the horizon and dozens of cartoon creatures and blocks floating among the skyscrapers, including a totem tower, a grey shark and a snow capped building, labelled DSNYC 1/1 2024.",
    "description": "A portrait format digital piece on a photograph inside a white border, captioned DSNYC 1/1 2024 at lower left and MATT CRUMP at lower right. A view from high in a glass tower, with the curved glass wall visible at the right edge, looking south over midtown to the downtown skyline, the rivers and the horizon, where a line of outlined cartoon clouds is drawn. Scattered through the real skyline are dozens of drawn objects: a tall totem pole of stacked faces with horns and wings at upper right, a grey shark shape with an eye at centre right, a skyscraper topped with drawn snow and icicles at lower left, a pink horned cone at lower left, a green striped cylinder at lower right, a pale blue cone, a blue cloth shape, small coloured cubes, a yellow fish, a blue paper plane, a cluster of pale blue mountains at upper left, and small creatures on rooftops. A copper roofed building fills the lower centre.",
    "impression": "Dominant species in NYC, the caption says, and the species seem to be the creatures: they have taken over the rooftops and the air above midtown like a migrating flock. The totem of faces beside the tower is the Superland totem poles come to Manhattan. A commission, and the grandest of the Scribbles, a whole city as a seek and find.",
